Mark a task in triage a duplicate of another: it is cancelled, its notes move to the original and the two are linked (maps to task.triage)

Usage: tasqx duplicate [OPTIONS] --of <ID> <REF>

Arguments:
  <REF>  short_id or UUID

Options:
      --json             Print the raw JSON API result instead of the human table
      --of <ID>          The task it repeats
      --holder <ID>      The claim holder acting, for a task claimed with `claim --holder` (D236)
      --theme <THEME>    Theme name (built-in nord|gruvbox|dracula|solarized|mono, or a user file). Overrides $TASQX_THEME and the config file (DESIGN.md §8)
      --force-claim      Act although another holder has a live claim on it (D236)
      --socket <SOCKET>  Local socket / named-pipe address of a tasqx daemon. Overrides $TASQX_SOCK. When a daemon is reachable, one-shot commands route through it (single writer); otherwise they run in-process. A set $TASQX_DB naming a different store than that daemon's is refused. Also selects the address for `daemon` and `watch`
      --no-daemon        Never route through a daemon; always run one-shot in-process (the pre-daemon behaviour). Escape hatch for scripts
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

EXAMPLES
  tasqx duplicate 12 --of 7    # cancels 12, moves its notes and dependents to 7 and links the two

NOTE  The proposal is cancelled, its notes move to the original (as `annotate --move` would) and a `duplicates` link joins the two. `tasqx undo` does not take it back: the newest event is the link, which it refuses by name (D238).

See also: triage · accept · decline        Full manual: tasqx manual
